  <!-- Why This Category Matters -->
  <section id="why-category-matters" style="padding: 4rem 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 2rem;">Why This Category Matters</h2>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        The global clothing manufacturing market reached $1.79 trillion in 2024 according to <a href="https://www.textilesresources.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">Textiles Resources</a>. It employs 3.62 billion people worldwide. Selecting the right manufacturer determines product quality, delivery reliability, and brand reputation.
      </p>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        In our experience working with 500+ brands across 30 countries, the wrong manufacturer choice costs brands an average of $50,000 in failed production runs. The right partner enables scalable growth and sustainable operations.
      </p>
      <div style="background: #0a0a0a; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <p style="font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem;">What is a clothing manufacturer?</p>
        <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">A clothing manufacturer produces garments from raw materials or fabrics. They handle cutting, sewing, finishing, and quality control. Manufacturers range from small workshops (50 workers) to massive facilities (10,000+ workers). They offer services from basic CMT (cut, make, trim) to full-package production including design and sourcing.</p>
      </div>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">
        The <a href="https://www.worldbank.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">World Bank</a> reports that Bangladesh alone exported $47 billion in garments in 2024. This scale means manufacturers with proper infrastructure can handle substantial volume while maintaining quality.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="methodology" style="padding: 4rem 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 2rem;">How We Ranked These Manufacturers</h2>
      <div style="background: #111; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 2rem;">
        <p style="color: #FFFFFF; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.7;">Our ranking methodology combines quantitative data with qualitative assessment from 27 years of Bangladesh RMG industry experience. We evaluated 427 manufacturers across five key criteria:</p>
        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem;">
          <div>
            <p style="font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #e00; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Compliance & Certifications (25%)</p>
            <p style="color: #aaa; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.6;">BSCI, SEDEX SMETA 4-pillar, WRAP, SA8000, OEKO-TEX Standard 100, GOTS 7.0 certification status and audit history from 2023-2025. Factories with multiple certifications scored highest.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p style="font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #e00; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Production Capacity & Technical Capability (25%)</p>
            <p style="color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.6;">Annual output capacity, production lines, workforce size, fabric sourcing, in-house sampling, pattern making, and product development. Full-service OEM facilities with vertical integration scored highest.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p style="font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #e00; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Quality Track Record (20%)</p>
            <p style="color: #aaa; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.6;">Repeat order rate, average client relationship duration (5+ years weighted highest), client diversity (no single client >40% of revenue), and on-time delivery performance.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p style="font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #e00; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Sustainability & Ethical Standards (20%)</p>
            <p style="color: #aaa; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.6;">Environmental certifications (LEED, green building investments), social compliance (Better Work participation, Accord/Alliance legacy), and sustainability commitments (ZDHC, Higg Index).</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p style="font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #e00; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Buyer Accessibility (10%)</p>
            <p style="color: #aaa; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.6;">Minimum order quantity tiers, ability to handle mixed-size runs, startup-friendly policies (300-500 piece MOQs scored highest), and communication responsiveness.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Key Buying Considerations -->
  <section id="buying-considerations" style="padding: 4rem 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 2rem;">Key Buying Considerations</h2>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        Selecting a clothing manufacturer requires evaluating multiple factors beyond price. In our 27 years of experience, brands that focus only on cost typically face quality issues and delivery delays.
      </p>
      <div style="background: #0a0a0a; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <p style="font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem;">1. MOQ Alignment</p>
        <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">Match manufacturer MOQ to your order volume. Startups need 300-500 piece minimums. Established brands can leverage volume discounts with 5,000+ piece orders. Never over-order to meet MOQs as this creates inventory risk.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background: #0a0a0a; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <p style="font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem;">2. Certification Verification</p>
        <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">Request certificate numbers and verify through official databases. GOTS certification can be checked at <a href="https://www.global-standard.org/database" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">global-standard.org/database</a>. OEKO-TEX verification is available at <a href="https://www.oeko-tex.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">oeko-tex.com</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background: #0a0a0a; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <p style="font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem;">3. Production Capacity vs. Your Growth</p>
        <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">Ensure the manufacturer can scale with you. A factory producing 50,000 pieces monthly may not prioritize your 500-piece order. Conversely, a small workshop cannot handle rapid scaling to 10,000 pieces.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background: #0a0a0a; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 2rem;">
        <p style="font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem;">4. Communication and Responsiveness</p>
        <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">Test communication before committing. Send inquiries and measure response times. Manufacturers taking 3+ days to reply will cause delays during production. Language barriers create quality issues in technical specifications.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Country Overview -->
  <section id="country-overview" style="padding: 4rem 0; background: #0a0a0a;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 2rem;">Country-by-Country Sourcing Overview</h2>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        Different countries excel at different product types and price points. The <a href="https://www.ilo.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">International Labour Organization</a> provides comprehensive data on labor conditions across manufacturing regions.
      </p>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <strong>Bangladesh</strong> leads in knitwear and denim production. The country offers 60-70% lower labor costs than China according to <a href="https://www.mckinsey.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">McKinsey & Company</a> research. Duty-free access to EU and UK markets through GSP provides additional cost advantages.
      </p>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <strong>Vietnam</strong> excels in complex garments and technical outerwear. The country's FTAs with EU and US provide tariff benefits. Vietnam has invested heavily in sustainable manufacturing infrastructure, making it attractive for eco-conscious brands.
      </p>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <strong>Turkey</strong> offers 7-10 day logistics to EU markets versus 35-45 days from Asia. This nearshoring advantage supports fast fashion production cycles. Turkey specializes in denim wash innovation and trend-responsive production.
      </p>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <strong>Portugal</strong> positions itself as premium "Made in Europe" production. The country specializes in high-quality knitwear and technical fabrics. While labor costs are higher, the EU Digital Product Passport readiness justifies the premium for European brands.
      </p>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">
        <strong>China</strong> maintains mass-market scale advantages. The country produces 35% of world garments according to <a href="https://www.statista.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">Statista</a>. China excels in complex technical garments and full-package production with rapid turnaround times.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Certifications Guide -->
  <section id="certifications" style="padding: 4rem 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 2rem;">Certifications and Compliance Guide</h2>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        Certifications verify manufacturer claims about quality, sustainability, and labor practices. The <a href="https://www.betterwork.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">ILO Better Work</a> program provides independent factory assessments.
      </p>
      <div style="background: #0a0a0a; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <p style="font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem;">GOTS 7.0 (Global Organic Textile Standard)</p>
        <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">Verifies organic fiber content from farm to finished product. Requires minimum 95% organic fibers for "GOTS Organic" label. Covers chemical processing restrictions and social compliance. Essential for EU Digital Product Passport compliance starting 2027.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background: #0a0a0a; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <p style="font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem;">OEKO-TEX Standard 100</p>
        <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">Tests final products for 100+ harmful substances. Required for CPSIA compliance in US children's wear. Certification levels range from Product Class I (babies) to Product Class IV (home textiles). Annual testing ensures ongoing compliance.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background: #0a0a0a; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <p style="font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem;">BSCI (Business Social Compliance Initiative)</p>
        <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">Covers 13 labor principles including fair wages, safe working conditions, no child labor, and freedom of association. Third-party audits occur every two years. Audit reports available with manufacturer permission.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background: #0a0a0a; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 2rem;">
        <p style="font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem;">WRAP (Worldwide Responsible Accredited Production)</p>
        <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">Certifies ethical manufacturing practices focusing on labor rights, workplace safety, and environmental management. Particularly important for UK buyers under Modern Slavery Act requirements. Certification database available at wrapcompliance.org.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What Changed in 2026 -->
  <section id="what-changed-2026" style="padding: 4rem 0; background: #0a0a0a;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 2rem;">What Changed in 2026</h2>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        The clothing manufacturing landscape shifted significantly in 2025-2026. New regulations and market dynamics changed how brands must approach sourcing.
      </p>
      <div style="background: #111; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <p style="font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem;">EU ESPR Digital Product Passport</p>
        <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">The EU Ecodesign for Sustainable Products Regulation entered force July 2024. Textiles face Digital Product Passport requirements starting 2027. Manufacturers need traceability systems to generate these passports. GOTS 7.0 certified factories have the required infrastructure in place.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background: #111; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <p style="font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem;">UFLPA Compliance</p>
        <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">The Uyghur Forced Labor Prevention Act establishes a rebuttable presumption that goods from Xinjiang, China are made with forced labor. Cotton sourcing requires specific documentation proving origin. Bangladesh manufacturers must trace cotton origin to avoid UFLPA enforcement.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background: #111; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <p style="font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem;">CBAM Carbon Costs</p>
        <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">The EU Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism imposes carbon costs on energy-intensive imports including textiles. Manufacturing powered by coal electricity faces higher costs than gas or renewable-powered factories. Bangladesh's coal dependency may increase costs versus cleaner energy countries.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background: #111; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding: 2rem;">
        <p style="font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Bangladesh LDC Graduation</p>
        <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">Bangladesh graduates from Least Developed Country status in 2026. This changes preferential trade agreements and may affect duty structures. Brands sourcing from Bangladesh should evaluate tariff impacts on their pricing models.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Case Study -->
  <section id="case-study" style="padding: 4rem 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 2rem;">Case Study: US Startup Sourcing 1,000 Hoodies</h2>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        A Los Angeles-based startup needed 1,000 hoodies for their first collection with a $5,000 budget. They required GOTS certification for their eco-conscious positioning and needed delivery within 60 days for their launch timeline.
      </p>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        The brand initially contacted Chinese manufacturers but found MOQs of 3,000 pieces exceeded their budget. They then approached several Bangladesh factories. Most required 5,000-piece minimums or lacked GOTS certification.
      </p>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        SDF Clothing met their requirements with 300-piece MOQ and GOTS 7.0 certification. The factory provided fabric sourcing from certified organic cotton mills, pattern making, and full production under one roof. This reduced communication overhead for the first-time brand owner.
      </p>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        Production took 35 days. Shipping via Chittagong port added 25 days to Los Angeles. Total cost came to $4,800 including fabric, production, and shipping. The hoodies arrived 10 days before the launch deadline, allowing time for quality inspection and photography.
      </p>
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">
        The brand has since placed three repeat orders, scaling to 2,500 pieces per order. The GOTS certification enabled them to list on premium sustainable marketplaces and justify higher retail pricing. This case demonstrates how low-MOQ certified production enables startup brand entry without quality or compliance compromises.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

